{"baseRefName":"docs/palette-ember-dusk-1-1","baseRefOid":"8f17f0e2f60f5af67871e4d21ab46689ad6e3fdb","body":"## What changed\n\nAnalytics page: sparklines, release markers, a 7-day average, a fixed contradictory tile, and a phone-overflow bug (stack 2/5; base: PR 1 branch).\n\n- **Floor tile contradicted itself.** The figure came from today's breakdown (`0%`) while the headline came from the whole series (\"every bucket folds into other\"). Both now read the same snapshot day (`namedBucketCount`), with a test tying them together.\n- **Sparklines** in the stat cards, drawn as server-rendered SVG (no chart library on the critical path). The scale starts at zero so a 4 → 5 wobble is not drawn as a cliff.\n- **Release markers** on the install chart for each published release inside the plotted window (re-filtered when the range toggle moves the left edge), plus a dashed **7-day average** computed over the full series then sliced.\n- **Copy:** \"opt-in / aggregates only\" was said four times on one page; once now. The permanent IST changeover paragraph is a native disclosure.\n- **`/analytics` had horizontal scroll on phones.** The npm chart's accessible table carried `sr-only` on the `<table>` itself; a table ignores the 1px width trick, stayed 320px wide and widened the layout viewport to 351px. The class is on a wrapper `div` now. (Pre-existing from #514.)\n- Two small links padded to a 24px target; wrapped 12px notes get ≥ 1.4 line-height.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nTested commit: this branch head. `rm -rf .next && bun run typecheck && bun run lint && bun run fmt:check && bun run test` in `apps/docs` → clean / 0 errors / clean / **298 pass, 0 fail**.\n\n- New pure helpers with unit tests: `namedBucketCount`, `rollingMean`, `releaseMarkers`, `sparklinePaths`. The tile test asserts a tile cannot say \"0% suppressed\" while naming nothing.\n- Browser, headless Chrome at 320 / 390 / 1440: `/analytics` scrollWidth was 351 at 320px before the fix and is 320 after; no other page overflowed.\n- Not exercised: a real-touch device, light mode (the site forces dark).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changeset: N/A (docs-only)\n- [x] `bun run guard`: N/A (no CLI manifest/changelog/changeset change in this PR)\n- [x] fmt / lint / test / typecheck pass locally (per package)\n- [ ] `bun run build` — run once on the top of the stack (PR 5), passes\n- [x] Live provider or Discord smokes skipped intentionally (docs only)\n","files":[{"path":"apps/docs/app/analytics/page.tsx","additions":2,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/app/styles/charts.css","additions":13,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/chart-installs.tsx","additions":74,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/npm-downloads.tsx","additions":19,"deletions":11,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/section-cards.tsx","additions":25,"deletions":7,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/share-bars.tsx","additions":4,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/sparkline.tsx","additions":51,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/trend-section.tsx","additions":14,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/trend-sync.tsx","additions":9,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/components/analytics/usage-panel.tsx","additions":15,"deletions":8,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/lib/analytics-derive.ts","additions":101,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/test/analytics-derive.test.ts","additions":70,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"headRefName":"docs/analytics-sparklines-release-markers","headRefOid":"444a049db0a2959b3f42eaf40f6b92f6905a8f0b","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":533,"reviewDecision":"","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-03T02:14:07Z","conclu